-- `Length`'s own operand-type rule: "value" must be an array or a string.
-- Anything else is core failing to do the work, and core answers with an
-- `Exception` like any other recipient — it does not end the frame that
-- emitted (2026-08-28; was `fail_emit_length_non_array.code`, which pinned
-- the old behaviour).
--
-- A field the particle does not carry is null, so `Length { }` is the same
-- particle as `Length { "value": null }` and produces the same failure. There
-- is no separate "you didn't supply it" complaint: emitting is not filling in
-- a form.
--
-- The messages are asserted in full because these two cannot be reached from
-- `tests/message_parity.rs` any more — that file provokes failures at the top
-- level, where these now answer instead of failing. This fixture is what
-- keeps the two backends' wording identical for them, since it runs under
-- both.
emit Length { "value": 5 } to core get n
assert n is Exception
assert n.source = "core"
assert n.message = "Length requires an array or string 'value', found a number"

emit Length { "value": null } to core get a
emit Length { } to core get b
assert a is Exception
assert b is Exception
assert a.message = b.message
assert a.message = "Length requires an array or string 'value', found a null"

-- The working path is untouched.
emit Length { "value": [1, 2, 3] } to core get ok
assert ok is LengthResult
assert ok.value = 3
